### What did I get myself into? ⚡
- Energy Company
- Senior Platform Engineering
- Different industry compared to M-DAQ
- Different in culture / mindset / purpose
- Friend working there as well

### What happened 🤔
- Didn't know that they are really focus on Decision Documents, from my previous organization, there was not a single Decision Docs and have never written one
- Hero Culture
    - Saw insecure setup and immediately tries to fix it
- Misalignment in Ideals & Goals
    - I didn't have a clear understanding of the ideals and goals of the team, the lead left the team shortly after I joined.
- Security Posture misfit
    - there was a misfit when I tried to introduce tighter security measures
- Too focus on suggesting change to better solutions but with not much impactful value
- Influence by colleagues and standards from Financial Institute and trying to push for similar security posture

### What I could have done better 🧗‍♂️

1. I should have used my probation time to focus on analyzing the existing infrastructure setup and question *WHY* it was done like this. Understand it from a technical perspective to the business needs. Document the reason down and best to always have a diagram drawn for any business flows.
    - Always good to question  *WHY* before suggesting change
    - Need to also understand the limitations that influence this design
2.
- Pragmatic Engineer
- Understand before execution
- Critical Analysis without any influence from team mates
- Managing Bias

### What I have done right and should continue doing
1. I took time to analyze the network flow that was designed and deployed by the ex-engineer. I trace the setup from source to destination, draw the architecture diagram, understand why it was designed in that day and present it to other colleagues to verify the flow.
    - There is always a reason why it was implemented that way.

2. Studied the CI/CD setup in Github Actions and understand the terraform structure
3. Request for knowledge transfer

### Support from colleagues 😊
